## 🚨 NON-NEGOTIABLE RULES

### **Thread Safety (ABSOLUTE)**

```cpp
AUDIO THREAD (Real-Time Priority - ~1ms budget):
  ❌ NEVER:
    - malloc, new, delete, std::vector::push_back
    - std::mutex, juce::CriticalSection (any lock)
    - std::cout, printf, DBG(), any logging
    - File I/O (open, read, write)
    - juce::MessageManager calls
    - ValueTree direct access
    
  ✅ ONLY:
    - std::atomic reads (lock-free)
    - Pre-allocated buffer access
    - Arithmetic operations
    - Read from audio files (pre-loaded)

UI THREAD:
  ✅ ALLOWED:
    - Skia rendering (no juce::Graphics)
    - ValueTree read/write
    - std::atomic reads
    - Memory allocations
    - JUCE MessageManager
    
  ❌ FORBIDDEN:
    - Audio processing
    - Blocking >16ms (causes frame drops)

BACKGROUND THREADS:
  ✅ ALLOWED:
    - Everything (file I/O, HTTP, allocations)
    
  ❌ FORBIDDEN:
    - Direct audio/UI data access (use MessageManager::callAsync)
```

### **Wayland Context Loss (CRITICAL)**

```cpp
// OpenGL context can be LOST at ANY time on Wayland
// MUST check EVERY frame

void renderFrame(int width, int height) {
    // 1. Validate context (REQUIRED)
    if (!grContext_ || grContext_->abandoned()) {
        recreateContext();
        return;
    }
    
    // 2. Query FBO (NEVER cache this!)
    GLint fbo;
    glGetIntegerv(GL_FRAMEBUFFER_BINDING, &fbo);
    
    // 3. Recreate surface on resize
    if (width != lastWidth_ || height != lastHeight_) {
        recreateSurface(width, height);
    }
    
    // 4. Now render
}

CAUSES OF CONTEXT LOSS:
- User switches workspace
- Window moved to different monitor
- Compositor restart
- System sleep/wake
- GPU driver reset
```

